<title>MEXICO: Mexico Bondes rate rises slightly at auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico Bondes rate rises slightly at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican government development bonds, or Bondes, rates rose 0.28 percentage points to 1.54 percent above the 28-day Cetes rate in Tuesday's primary auction, dealers estimated.</p>
<p>The 728-day Bondes were assigned at 97.58831 pesos.</p>
<p>Demand for the bondes was 2.881 billion pesos, compared with the 900 million offered by the Banco de Mexico.</p>
<p>- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559</p>
</text>
